    "body": "# Bug report\n\n### Bug description:\n\nLeakSanitizer detects memory leaks in the readline module when running `test_audit`.\n\n### Affected Code\nFour functions in `Modules/readline.c`:\n- line 298: `PyUnicode_FSConverter` call https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/b2f9fb9db29296410f76009ac65cf81afa8a92a9/Modules/readline.c#L278-L316\n- line 342: `PyUnicode_FSConverter` call https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/b2f9fb9db29296410f76009ac65cf81afa8a92a9/Modules/readline.c#L320-L366\n- line 399: `PyUnicode_FSConverter` call https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/b2f9fb9db29296410f76009ac65cf81afa8a92a9/Modules/readline.c#L371-L424\n- line 255: `PyUnicode_FSConverter` call https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/b2f9fb9db29296410f76009ac65cf81afa8a92a9/Modules/readline.c#L237-L276\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\nBuild:\n```bash\nCC=clang CXX=clang++ ./configure --disable-optimizations --with-pydebug --with-address-sanitizer && make -j$(nproc)\n```\n\nRun:\n```bash\n./python -X dev -X showrefcount -m test test_audit -j0\n```\n\n### Result\nLeakSanitizer reports 4 memory leaks of 75 bytes each (300 bytes total). Full logs attached as .log files.\n\nSummary from LeakSanitizer:\n```\nSUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: 300 byte(s) leaked in 4 allocation(s).\n```\n\nAll leaks originate from `PyUnicode_FSConverter` calls in the affected functions.\n\n### CPython versions tested on:\n\n3.14, 3.15, CPython main branch\n\n### Operating systems tested on:\n\nLinux\n\n<!-- gh-linked-prs -->\n### Linked PRs\n* gh-140400\n* gh-140403\n<!-- /gh-linked-prs -->\n",
